  "saferAlternatives": [
    "Start with get_context, read_messages, list_pending_orders, read_transfer, and list_wakes for read-only inspection; note that get_updates with participant_id advances that participant's signal cursor.",
    "prepare_transfer declares size_bytes and sha256 upfront; the hub streams the PUT upload to a temporary file and rejects size or SHA-256 mismatches before complete_transfer can publish the offer to recipients.",
    "Inspect transfer metadata and sha256 with read_transfer before calling fetch_transfer, which records a download receipt and issues a short-lived download ticket plus a local SHA-256 verification command.",
    "Install ForgeLoopBridge in a dedicated Python environment and configure the installed forgeloopbridge-mcp console script over stdio; python or uv wrappers remain on Guard's ordinary policy."
  ]
